  "non_canonical_note": "y = p+2..p+18 with either sign bit, restricted to the y values (3,4,5,6,9,10,14,15,16,18 after reduction) that decode to curve points; the other values do not decode. These points are not small-order, so no signature can be built that verifies under them (their discrete logs are unknown). Every verifier must reject a non-canonical (y >= p) public key and a non-canonical R: the public key explicitly, and R because it is compared byte-for-byte against the canonical re-encoding. The cross-implementation check is the predicate and the verdict on these encodings, in both the public-key and R positions."
